2e506c6e6119ccfd747f9f76c781b5a661e273fcbd" "basis" 1259 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(3x)}{3}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c1681a73dd1fc724fb66e2e506c6e6119ccfd747f9f76c781b5a661e273fcbd" "basis" 1259 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c1681a73dd1fc724fb66e2e506c6e6119ccfd747f9f76c781b5a661e273fcbd" "basis" 1259 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c1681a73dd1fc724fb66e2e506c6e6119ccfd747f9f76c781b5a661e273fcbd" "basis" 1259 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "31e77975055356dfb2474618c3afed650e3c461761c728a631bc7a95a0837710" "basis" 1259 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114084" "field" "selection" "attrib